From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: no taskbar button flickers for a Linux window just closed

A framed Linux window closed (its program's window destroyed) and its
frame and taskbar button went at once -- but the compositor's window list
read at the taskbar's next tick may have been asked for just before, and
still named it: a stand-in and a taskbar button were made for a window no
longer there, and went again at the read after. A button flickered on the
taskbar after a Linux window closed, and a test looking for the frame
gone could find the stand-in (linuxembed-gate's "the frame stayed", now
and then).

A list is not believed about a framed window that has just gone (for two
seconds; a new window given the same X id meanwhile is framed when that
is over).

Test: test/linuxembed-gate.sh 8 (the list left naming the closed window a
moment longer, a probe watching for any SgLinuxWindow meanwhile).
Mutant SG_MUTANT_GONE_XWIN_BUTTON (programs/explorer/systray.c) fails it.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1752,6 +1752,33 @@
 
 static void sg_remove_xwin_button( struct taskbar_button *win );
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: a framed Linux window just closed (its program's window
+ * destroyed): the compositor's list read at the next tick may have been asked
+ * for before, and still name it -- a button was made for it, a stand-in for
+ * a window no longer there, and gone again at the read after: a taskbar
+ * button flickering after every Linux window closed. Such a list is not
+ * believed about it for a moment. */
+static struct { unsigned long id; DWORD time; } sg_gone_xwins[8];
+
+static void sg_xwin_gone( unsigned long id )
+{
+    static unsigned int next;
+    sg_gone_xwins[next % ARRAY_SIZE(sg_gone_xwins)].id = id;
+    sg_gone_xwins[next % ARRAY_SIZE(sg_gone_xwins)].time = GetTickCount();
+    next++;
+}
+
+static BOOL sg_xwin_just_gone( unsigned long id )
+{
+    unsigned int i;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_GONE_XWIN_BUTTON
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sg_gone_xwins); i++)
+        if (sg_gone_xwins[i].id == id && GetTickCount() - sg_gone_xwins[i].time < 2000) return TRUE;
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 static LRESULT CALLBACK sg_linux_standin_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wp, LPARAM lp )
 {
     static UINT end_msg;
@@ -1831,6 +1858,7 @@
             else ShowWindow( hwnd, SW_SHOWNA );
             return 0;
         case WM_SG_EMBED_GONE:
+            sg_xwin_gone( win->embedded );
             sg_remove_xwin_button( win );
             return 0;
         case WM_ERASEBKGND:
@@ -2247,6 +2275,7 @@
         LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( win, &taskbar_buttons, struct taskbar_button, entry )
             if (win->xwin == id || win->embedded == id) break;
         if (&win->entry != &taskbar_buttons && win->embedded) continue;   /* a Wine window now */
+        if (&win->entry == &taskbar_buttons && sg_xwin_just_gone( id )) continue;   /* a list older than its going */
         if (&win->entry == &taskbar_buttons)
         {
             HICON icon = sg_xwin_icon( class );
